From: Pi <pi@local>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: advertise MAX_AMSDU on every band

ath12k derives IEEE80211_HT_CAP_MAX_AMSDU from the firmware VHT capability
word.  Radios that are limited to 2.4 GHz report no VHT capabilities at
all, so the bit was missing on band 1 while band 2 (5 GHz) advertised it.

On the IPQ53xx MLO group both radios share one wiphy, so the OpenWrt
wireless configuration helper ORs the HT capabilities of all bands
together and applies the result to each radio.  The 2.4 GHz radio then
asks hostapd for MAX-AMSDU-7935, which hostapd validates against that
band's own capabilities, fails, and disables the BSS:

  Driver does not support configured HT capability [MAX-AMSDU-7935]
  wlan0: interface state COUNTRY_UPDATE->DISABLED

A-MSDU aggregation up to 7935 bytes is supported by the hardware on all
bands, including HE-only 2.4 GHz operation, so advertise the capability
unconditionally instead of gating it on the VHT capability word.

Signed-off-by: Pi <pi@local>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -8428,8 +8428,10 @@ ath12k_mac_setup_ht_cap(struct ieee80211
 	if (ar_ht_cap & WMI_HT_CAP_L_SIG_TXOP_PROT)
 		ht_cap.cap |= IEEE80211_HT_CAP_LSIG_TXOP_PROT;
 
-	if (ar_vht_cap & WMI_VHT_CAP_MAX_MPDU_LEN_MASK)
-		ht_cap.cap |= IEEE80211_HT_CAP_MAX_AMSDU;
+	/* A-MSDUs up to 7935 bytes are supported on every band, including
+	 * 2.4 GHz HE-only radios which report no VHT capabilities at all.
+	 */
+	ht_cap.cap |= IEEE80211_HT_CAP_MAX_AMSDU;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ar->num_rx_chains; i++) {
 		if (rate_cap_rx_chainmask & BIT(i))
